
<Defs xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="rimworld ../DefsSchema.xsd" xmlns="rimworld">

	<!--
		One shared "mamono meat" for every mamono race that butchers into meat.

		The def lives in this mod, not in a species mod, so the whole family can share the
		same item - the same reason PMM_MamonoCorpses lives here.

		Why a species needs to name it: vanilla gives each race its own meat.
		ThingDefGenerator_Meat.ImpliedMeatDefs runs from DefGenerator.
		GenerateImpliedDefs_PreResolve and builds Meat_<defName> for every pawn def with
		hasMeat and hasCorpse that names no <specificMeatDef> and no <useMeatFrom>, then
		assigns race.meatDef to the result. It never checks whether meatDef was already
		set, so even a race that inherits Human's Meat_Human gets a brand-new one.

		Two fields redirect that, and they are not equivalent. A plain <meatDef> does
		work: it is a cross-reference, and the pass that resolves cross-references
		(ResolveAllWantedCrossReferences, called from the same PreResolve method) runs
		after the generator, so the XML value is applied last and wins. What a plain
		<meatDef> does not do is stop the race's own generated def from being created and
		registered, unused. <specificMeatDef> is part of the generator's skip test, so it
		does both: RaceProperties.ResolveReferencesSpecial points race.meatDef at it, and
		no dead per-race def exists. That is why the eleven reptiles and the seven
		elemental mamono use it: one meat in the butcher menu, in the food filter and in
		the stockpile, with nothing generated behind them.

		The field values below are what the generator would have written for a humanlike
		race, so nothing a player can see changes except the item's identity:
		- MarketValue 0.8 is Human's own meatMarketValue, which every mamono race
		  inherited, so a butchered mamono is still worth exactly what it was.
		- sourceDef keeps the meat classified as HUMANLIKE meat.
		  FoodUtility.GetMeatSourceCategory reads that one field, and everything else
		  follows from it: the cannibalism thoughts, the Ideology "ate human meat"
		  precepts, and the moods of anyone who eats the meat or a meal made with it.
		  Left empty, mamono meat would stop counting as humanlike to every eater.
		- Untinted vanilla human meat art, which is what the per-race defs drew: no
		  mamono race sets <meatColor>, so those defs were untinted too.
		- No specialThoughtDirect and no specialThoughtAsIngredient: the generator copies
		  those from the race's flesh type, and Human's Normal flesh type leaves both
		  empty.
		- MeatAmount is untouched - it stays on the race, so a basilisk still gives more
		  meat than a gnome.

		Deliberately NOT on this def: slime mamono (slime jelly), insect mamono (vanilla
		Meat_Megaspider, which their flesh gene and the insect meals are built around) and
		the dryad mamono (WoodLog). Each of those names its own def in <specificMeatDef>.
	-->
	<ThingDef>
		<defName>PMM_MamonoMeat</defName>
		<label>mamono meat</label>
		<description>Raw, red meat cut from a mamono's body. It rots like any other raw meat and can be cooked into any meal.\n\nMamono are human enough that eating their meat counts as eating human meat.</description>
		<thingClass>ThingWithComps</thingClass>
		<category>Item</category>
		<drawerType>MapMeshOnly</drawerType>
		<resourceReadoutPriority>Middle</resourceReadoutPriority>
		<useHitPoints>true</useHitPoints>
		<selectable>true</selectable>
		<altitudeLayer>Item</altitudeLayer>
		<stackLimit>75</stackLimit>
		<tickerType>Rare</tickerType>
		<comps>
			<li Class="CompProperties_Forbiddable" />
			<li Class="CompProperties_Rottable">
				<daysToRotStart>2</daysToRotStart>
				<rotDestroys>true</rotDestroys>
			</li>
			<!-- The harbinger tree eats it, the way it eats the meat the game generates
			     for every other race. -->
			<li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Anomaly">
				<compClass>CompHarbingerTreeConsumable</compClass>
			</li>
		</comps>
		<alwaysHaulable>true</alwaysHaulable>
		<drawGUIOverlay>true</drawGUIOverlay>
		<rotatable>false</rotatable>
		<pathCost>14</pathCost>
		<possessionCount>5</possessionCount>
		<healthAffectsPrice>false</healthAffectsPrice>
		<socialPropernessMatters>true</socialPropernessMatters>
		<graphicData>
			<texPath>Things/Item/Resource/MeatFoodRaw/Meat_Human</texPath>
			<graphicClass>Graphic_StackCount</graphicClass>
		</graphicData>
		<statBases>
			<MarketValue>0.8</MarketValue>
			<MaxHitPoints>60</MaxHitPoints>
			<DeteriorationRate>6</DeteriorationRate>
			<Mass>0.03</Mass>
			<Flammability>0.5</Flammability>
			<Nutrition>0.05</Nutrition>
			<FoodPoisonChanceFixedHuman>0.02</FoodPoisonChanceFixedHuman>
			<Beauty>-4</Beauty>
		</statBases>
		<ingestible>
			<foodType>Meat</foodType>
			<preferability>RawBad</preferability>
			<tasteThought>AteRawFood</tasteThought>
			<ingestEffect>EatMeat</ingestEffect>
			<ingestSound>RawMeat_Eat</ingestSound>
			<sourceDef>Human</sourceDef>
		</ingestible>
		<thingCategories>
			<li>MeatRaw</li>
		</thingCategories>
	</ThingDef>

</Defs>
